[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-PLAN-WP-18
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Scale simulation, resource limits and measured parallel execution
STATEMENT: >>>
Published benchmarks include source/tool/configuration hashes, baseline timings, repeat distributions and correctness checks; demonstrate actual worker scaling or explicitly report no gain.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Inferred planning acceptance for WP-18, P2, relative scope XL. Major throughput and scale slices implemented and verified under VS-RTL-NARROW64-001 (PR #41), VS-RTL-TWOSTATE-001 (PR #42), VS-RTL-TARGETS-001 (PR #43: C# and safe Rust codegen) and VS-RTL-SCALE-001 (opt-in RtlDesignLimits.Large / --large-design with 65,536 signals and 1M-word memories). Head-to-head benchmarks against Verilator 5.055 (-O3 and -O3 -flto) on DspFir and surelog_fifo verified bit-for-bit identical checksums. Hierarchical compilation and multi-threaded structural DAG partitioning remain open. Dependencies: WP-01, WP-04, WP-07. Product IDs: VS-QUAL-001, VS-RTL-NARROW64-001, VS-RTL-TWOSTATE-001, VS-RTL-TARGETS-001, VS-RTL-SCALE-001. GitHub issue: https://github.com/jeffadickson/VeloSim/issues/19. Library evaluation: LIB-03, LIB-08, LIB-14, LIB-15, LIB-18.
<<<
